    "available_at": "2026-11-16T23:10:06.003289+00:00",
    "body": "Exus Renewables North America, an independent owner, developer, and operator of utility-scale renewable energy and energy storage projects, has announced the closing of $345 million in senior secured holding company financing led by Goldman Sachs Alternatives. The financing will support construction costs and the development of new projects across Exus’ growing U.S. portfolio of wind, solar and battery storage assets.\nThe financing announced November 12 builds on an active year for Exus , including the closing of a $400 million senior secured corporate credit facility in December and approximately $356 million in project-level construction financing for its Highland North and Cambria wind projects in Pennsylvania in July . With more than 800 MW operating or under construction and a total portfolio exceeding 6 GW, Exus continues to advance its project pipeline amid rising U.S. electricity demand.\n“We have projects moving forward and a deep pipeline behind them, and this financing lets us keep that momentum going,” said Jim Spencer, president and CEO of Exus Renewables North America. “The support from Goldman Sachs Alternatives reflects confidence in our team and our projects, and gives us the flexibility to keep building and bring new generation online where it’s needed.”\n“Exus has established a strong platform for developing and operating utility-scale renewable energy projects,” said Vikas Agrawal, managing director and co-head of Energy Transition Climate Credit at Goldman Sachs Alternatives. “We’re pleased to support its continued investment in new energy infrastructure as electricity demand grows across the United States.”\nPEI Global Partners served as financial advisor to Exus on the transaction. Latham & Watkins LLP served as legal counsel to Exus, while Vinson & Elkins LLP served as legal counsel to Goldman Sachs Alternatives.\n—This content was contributed by the communications team for Exus Renewables North America .\nTagged in:\nbatteries\nEnergy storage\nExus\nExus Renewables North America\nfinancing\nGoldman Sachs Alternatives\nsolar\nwind\nSept. 28—30, 2026\nWashington, D.C.\nRegister Now\nExplore this topic and more — live at Experience POWER. The power industry's most urgent decisions are being made right now. Be in the room where they happen.\nView Conference Program",
